      "problem": "Express $\\left(2^{-4}\\right)^{2}$ as a base raised to a single, positive exponent.",
      "worked_solution": "To raise a power to another power, we simply multiply the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\left(2^{-4}\\right)^{2}=2^{(-4)\\cdot 2}=2^{-8}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate $2^{-8},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(2)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n2^{-8} = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{8}\n$$",
